cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use meerkat or its results, please cite it as below.
title: Meerkat
type: software
abstract: >-
  Meerkat is a triage tool for multi-detector SOC alert data. It groups Wazuh,
  Suricata and log-anomaly alerts into sessions and same-day families, then ranks
  the families so that one day of review covers as many distinct attack steps as
  possible. Under leave-one-environment-out evaluation on the AIT Alert Data Set,
  a review budget of 10 families per day reaches 58 of 60 reachable attack
  windows, against 33 for the detectors' own severity ranking.
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Jiacheng
    email: jiacheng.wang@eurecom.fr
    affiliation: EURECOM
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/jiacwng/meerkat'
keywords:
  - alert triage
  - security operations center
  - intrusion detection
  - alert prioritization
  - machine learning
  - security operations
  - MITRE ATT&CK
  - Wazuh
  - Suricata
  - log anomaly detection
